module gunbc.qualified_pipe_callee_seed_growth

import std.decl_ref { DeclarationRef, WholeDeclaration }
import std.types { String }
import gunbc.roadmap_model { RoadmapNodeId }
import gunbc.seed_growth { SeedGrowthJustification }

data qualified_pipe_callee_seed_growth_note: String = "Seed-growth obligation for the discriminating evidence behind the qualified-callee-in-pipe-position repair. It is homed here, beside the obligation it declares, rather than inside gunbc.seed_growth_admission, which owns the ROSTER and the join and would otherwise accumulate every lane's rows in the module that adjudicates them.\n\nWHAT THE CHANGE ITSELF WAS, because the growth is only defensible relative to it: v1.compiler.parse parse_pipe_rhs consumed exactly one identifier after the pipe arrow, so a qualified callee in pipe position had its ROOT SEGMENT lowered as a method on the receiver -- the remaining segments folding on top as field access -- while the same callee in ordinary call position resolved correctly. One authored denotation, two answers, decided by syntactic position. The repair consumes the whole dotted path and hands the leading segments to the qualifier spine that v1.compiler.infer's qualified_direct_call arm already reads, so both positions reach ONE resolution path rather than two.\n\nWHY THE TEST FILE IS ENUMERATED AT ALL: seed_growth_forward_freeze_policy_note names 'hand-written src/v1 Rust' with exactly two exclusions -- deleting existing Rust, and netting deletions against additions -- and neither exempts tests. gunbc.stage0_rust_source_lifecycle_scaffold declares rust_source_prefix_stage0_test as 'src/v1/stage0/tests/' and lists it among the discovery prefix hints, so the stage0 test tree is a DECLARED Rust source class rather than an unclassified one. The precedent this row follows in shape is gunbc.parse_refusal_location_seed_growth, authored one lane earlier for the same reason.\n\nNO NEW UNCITABLE ITEM: all seven additions are free functions, so each is nameable as a DeclarationRef with WholeDeclaration. No struct, no impl block, and therefore none of the impl-method class gunbc.seed_growth_admission reports separately in seed_growth_uncitable_item_keys."

data qualified_pipe_callee_seed_growth_justification: SeedGrowthJustification = SeedGrowthJustification {
  hand_authored_declarations: [
    DeclarationRef {
      module_path: "v1_compiler.tests.qualified_callee_pipe_position",
      decl_name: "provider_source",
      field: WholeDeclaration
    },
    DeclarationRef {
      module_path: "v1_compiler.tests.qualified_callee_pipe_position",
      decl_name: "diagnostics_of",
      field: WholeDeclaration
    },
    DeclarationRef {
      module_path: "v1_compiler.tests.qualified_callee_pipe_position",
      decl_name: "diagnostics_for_consumer",
      field: WholeDeclaration
    },
    DeclarationRef {
      module_path: "v1_compiler.tests.qualified_callee_pipe_position",
      decl_name: "qualified_callee_in_call_position_resolves",
      field: WholeDeclaration
    },
    DeclarationRef {
      module_path: "v1_compiler.tests.qualified_callee_pipe_position",
      decl_name: "qualified_callee_in_pipe_position_resolves",
      field: WholeDeclaration
    },
    DeclarationRef {
      module_path: "v1_compiler.tests.qualified_callee_pipe_position",
      decl_name: "dotted_pipe_callee_without_application_is_method_then_field",
      field: WholeDeclaration
    },
    DeclarationRef {
      module_path: "v1_compiler.tests.qualified_callee_pipe_position",
      decl_name: "bare_callee_in_pipe_position_is_unchanged",
      field: WholeDeclaration
    }
  ],
  reason: "WHY RUST RATHER THAN A .dag WITNESS, and it is a REACHABILITY limit rather than a preference: the two builtins a .dag witness would use for this subject -- compile_dag_rust_emit_check and compile_dag_diagnostic_census -- both resolve their synthetic source through v1_compiler.cli_run build_module_path_index_from_witness_roots, which walks the live tree. A witness written on either declares ReadsLiveTree and is therefore DECLINED by the required floor's home policy rather than executed, which DESIGN's CI section already records for the compile-clean witness family: discovered, counted, and answering nothing. Authoring one more such witness would add a name to that family without adding an assertion that runs, which DESIGN 4b calls worse than absent because it is cited as coverage. compile_sources takes its sources in memory, so the evidence here reads no repository file and needs no module index -- it is hermetic by construction, and it executes today under cargo test.\n\nWHAT THIS DOES NOT CLAIM: cargo test is a LOCAL check in this repository, removed from CI by operator ruling 2026-07-11. So this evidence executes on demand and is not a merge gate, and no gate closes this class until a required phase emits over a closure -- the compile re-add DESIGN names as this class's restoration trigger. Stating that here rather than letting the row imply CI coverage is the point of writing it down.\n\nWHY IT IS ADMITTED AGAINST THE v1 FREEZE: gunbc.v1_maintenance_standing v1_seed_standing admits by PURPOSE -- does the change serve the v2 self-host program. Under namespace-only resolution every callee becomes qualified, so a qualified callee in pipe position moves from rare to ordinary; the branch measured this class at roughly 119 of its 410 diagnostics. A parser that answers one denotation two ways by position is a direct tax on that program.\n\nHAND-ITEM DELTA: +7, all seven citable above and enumerated rather than counted, all seven in the ONE new file. src/v1/02_parse.dag is a .dag change and adds no hand item; its Rust mirror is generated, so its disposition is generated-surface regeneration and listing it would net a generated change into a hand census.",
  owning_dissolution_lane: "v1-hand-queue-drain" as RoadmapNodeId,
  trigger: "Delete all seven when a required phase compiles a multi-module closure from fixture-authored sources -- the compile re-add on the queue the floor cut created. At that point the same three cases are authorable as .dag witnesses over in-memory sources and execute in the floor, so the assertions move to the substrate unchanged and the Rust file is redundant rather than merely unfashionable. What does NOT dissolve them is the single-source compile builtins gaining a second caller: those read the live tree, so a witness on them is declined and would retire executing evidence in favour of a name. What does NOT dissolve them either is this defect being fixed -- the fix is what they guard.",
  current_boundary: "src/v1/02_parse.dag parse_pipe_rhs; src/v1/02_parse.dag parse_pipe_callee_rest; src/v1/02_parse.dag pipe_callee_path_is_applied; src/v1/stage0/tests/qualified_callee_pipe_position.rs; dag/gunbc/qualified_pipe_callee_seed_growth.dag"
}
